WEBVTT

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.310
When people and AI work together well,
you gain more than speed.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.330
At The Only Constant
we see how to make that happen.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.200
Many AI implementations fail
because organisations mostly look

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.100
at the technology
and the cost savings.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:25.000
Often the first step
is investing in AI tools,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.640
without really looking at what employees need
or what actually helps customers.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:34.580
AI then gets stuck
on top of existing processes.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.720
But then AI makes a bad process
faster at best, not better.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:45.620
Real change starts with employees
and customers, not with technology.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.300
Your employees know
where today's work gets stuck

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.460
and which tasks
take far too much time.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.520
And your customers show you
where your service can improve.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.800
What AI does and what people do
is a design decision.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.040
Organisations run
on a huge number of processes.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.600
Take one process
and break it into small steps,

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.900
and for each step you can see
which data goes in,

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.560
what is done with it
and what comes out.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:23.350
In that step you also decide
what people do and what AI does.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:29.210
The card set solves that problem.
It gives people a vocabulary for AI.

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:35.000
Looking at a process in their organisation,
people can use the cards themselves

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:40.480
to see which problem
AI solves within that process.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.000
After the workshop
we can get started right away.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.500
Within two weeks
there can be a working solution.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:53.760
One that runs on the client's data and systems
and can be used straight away.
